-- EXPECT-ERROR: Actor.introspect
-- Unforgeable local references (2026-09-22, distributed-deploys build step 2,
-- specs/progress/2026-09-22-dd-step02-unforgeable-references.md).
--
-- `pid_of_int` turns an integer anyone can write down into a Pid, so a
-- program that holds no Pid could still message any actor. The raw builtin
-- is now internal to the standard library (`Typecheck_builtins.stdlib_only`);
-- user code goes through `Actor.pid_from_int(c, n)`, whose
-- `c : Cap(Actor.Introspect)` only `Actor.introspect(io : Cap(IO))` mints.
-- The error names that minting function, so the fix is in the message.
--
-- Accept companion: accept/t291, the same program with the cap minted in
-- `main` and forwarded.
mod ForgesAPid do
  needs IO.Console

  fn main(_c : Cap(IO.Console)) do
    println(bool_to_string(is_alive(pid_of_int(7))))
  end
end
